y = capacity\n        self.ttl = ttl\n        self.clock = clock\n        self.data = OrderedDict()\n        self._expiries = OrderedDict()\n\n    def put(self, k, v):\n        if self.capacity <= 0:\n            return\n        now = self.clock()\n        self._purge(now)\n        if k in self.data:\n            del self.data[k]\n            del self._expiries[k]\n        while len(self.data) >= self.capacity:\n            old_k, _ = self.data.popitem(last=False)\n            del self._expiries[old_k]\n        self.data[k] = (v, now)\n        self._expiries[k] = now\n\n    def get(self, k, default=None):\n        entry = self.data.get(k)\n        if entry is None:\n            return default\n        v, t = entry\n        if self.clock() - t >= self.ttl:\n            del self.data[k]\n            del self._expiries[k]\n            return default\n        self.data.move_to_end(k)\n        return v\n\n    def _purge(self, now):\n        while self._expiries:\n            k, t = next(iter(self._expiries.items()))\n            if now - t < self.ttl:\n                break\n            del self._expiries[k]\n            del self.data[k]\n```\n\nWait: `if entry is None` — value could be None if stored; `data.get(k)` returns None both when missing and when stored value is None (tuple (None, t) is not None, so fine! tuple is not None). Actually data.get(k) returns the tuple; tuple never None. Good. But cleaner: `if k not in self.data: return default`.\n\nEdge: `popitem(last=False)` on empty → error; but while condition ensures len >= capacity >= 1, so len >= 1. Good.\n\nEdge: capacity is e.g. 2 but len already... fine.\n\nNow about `_purge` removing data entries: all keys in _expiries should be in data. Keep them in sync.\n\nRecursion/position: get's expiry check uses `self.clock()` once.\n\nOne more consideration on get and recency: \"Successful get refreshes recency but not expiry\" — we move_to_end in data. Correct.\n\n\"Updating a key refreshes expiry and recency\": de